    "body": "Wire the fused device-side input normalization into MiniMax-M3, following the Qwen2-VL integration pattern:\r\n\r\n- Set supports_mm_device_do_normalize on MiniMaxM3SparseForConditionalGeneration (nvidia and amd variants) so the flag defaults to on.\r\n- Build the input norm via build_mm_input_norm and apply it at the MiniMaxVLVisionTransformer entry; raw uint8 pixels are normalized on device, and the pre-casts in _process_image_input/_process_video_input are removed since the norm layer owns the dtype conversion.\r\n\r\nThe vendored MiniMaxM3VL image/video processors already emit uint8 pixel_values when do_normalize/do_rescale are off, so no processor changes are needed. With the flag off, IdentityInputNorm reproduces the previous behavior bit-identically.\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: Kimi\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\n---\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Essential Elements of an Effective PR Description Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [ ] The purpose of the PR, such as \"Fix some issue (link existing issues this PR will resolve)\".\r\n- [ ] The test plan, such as providing test command.\r\n- [ ] The test results, such as pasting the results comparison before and after, or e2e results\r\n- [ ] (Optional) The necessary documentation update, such as updating `supported_models.md` and `examples` for a new model.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n",
